The accepted common profile now has six smooth background coefficients, nonnegative W, SH/L asymmetry, isotropic size/strain, and weak [110] texture; replay is stable at Rwp ≈ 6.36%. I’m re-challenging CuO, two room-temperature WO₃ polymorphs, and the other Cu–W–O stoichiometries against that same profile, starting with scale only as required.

