The strain-only branch has already reduced χ² from ~82,500 to ~43,200 without damping or bounds, nearly recovering the full accepted fit. This cleanly identifies microstrain—not crystallite size—as the needed phase-dependent width term for CuWO₄; I’m completing its replay, then I’ll add and replay-test the WO₃ strain separately.

